This change in NSDeviceStatusHandler.kt fixes the issue for me, but not sure if it's a proper fix. I'm not able to at first glance locate the root cause to why Dash is reporting battery.

```
            pump.battery?.percent?.let {
                if (it > 0) { // ignore 0 or invalid
                    deviceStatusPumpData.isPercent = true
                    deviceStatusPumpData.percent = it
                }
            }
```
